        <body>
            <div xml:id="d235">

                <pb facs="0270" n="258" sameAs="frus:frus1940v03/pg258"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">700.00116 M.E./141</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Amtorg Trading Corporation, New York, N.
                        Y.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-03-20">March 20, 1940</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sirs</hi>: The receipt is acknowledged of your
                    letter of March 14, 1940, with further reference to certain policies of this
                    Government in respect to the exportation of certain articles and commodities. It
                    is noted that you are aware of the policies in question. It would be greatly
                    appreciated if you would inform me at your earliest convenience whether the
                    Department is correct in its assumption that, as you are aware of these
                    policies, you will act in conformity thereto.</p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Joseph</hi> C. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Green</hi>
                    </signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Chief, Division of Controls</hi>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
